From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 21:10:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03340/11362] [outer-loop] arc: coordinated redesign piece 2 --
 divergence-tolerant TTT solve loop

The exact-match plan_and_execute HALTS on pred!=obs, so a useful-but-imperfect learned model (TTT CNN
~0.55 cell-recall, exact-grid ~0) can never drive a solve even after the cell-recall gate (piece 1)
trusts it. Piece 2 (arc_ttt_solve_loop.ttt_solve): instead of halting on divergence, OBSERVE the real
transition, LEARN from the surprise (refit), and REPLAN from the actual state -- each divergence is a
correction, not a dead end. Composes piece 1 (cell-recall-gated TTT engine) + piece 2 (replan-on-
divergence execution) + a NAIVE explore placeholder for piece 3 (directed exploration to first-win,
the binding constraint). Honest scope: plan_in_model needs an OBSERVED win-state, so on games where
exploration never triggers a first level-up the loop has no goal -> this piece moves deepening/efficiency
where a win is reachable and exposes the exploration-to-first-win wall on the rest. Measured next.

